      "properties": {
        "draftsman": "comfy-draftsman"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Inputs\n\nLoad your source image/media here.\n\nSet the image size (width / height / batch) here.\n\n| knob | now | range / choices | effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| batch_size (EmptyTrellis2LatentStructure #87) | 1 | 1-4096 | How many images render per run - more takes proportionally longer and more VRAM. |\n| width (ImageCropToMask #312) | 1024 | 64-4096 | Output width in pixels - usually needs to match the model's trained resolution bucket, or composition degrades. |\n| height (ImageCropToMask #312) | 1024 | 64-4096 | Output height in pixels - same caveat as width. |"
      ],
      "title": "Inputs",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 324,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        745.0,
        -229.0
      ],
      "size": [
        380.0,
        189.0
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "draftsman": "comfy-draftsman"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Models\n\nSwap models here to change the whole look.\n\n| knob | now | range / choices | effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| shift (ModelSamplingSD3 #108) | 5 | 0.0-100.0 | Shifts the noise schedule - affects how detail resolves across steps; usually a per-model tuned constant. |\n| cfg (CFGOverride #199) | 1 | 0.0-100.0 | Higher CFG follows the prompt more literally but can oversaturate or burn; lower is more creative but may ignore the prompt. |\n| cfg (CFGOverride #279) | 1 | 0.0-100.0 | Higher CFG follows the prompt more literally but can oversaturate or burn; lower is more creative but may ignore the prompt. |"
      ],
      "title": "Models",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
